# Components

The site is small. There are ~8 components total. Build them as
**framework-agnostic** primitives that consume tokens. Names match the
class names in `/handoff/reference/styles.css`.

## 1. `<Mast>` — masthead (every page)

- Two-column grid: wordmark left, `/nav` right.
- Wordmark renders the brand: `▮ ripblog`. The `▮` is a `::before` glyph in
  `var(--color-accent)`; do not use an SVG.
- `<nav>` has 5 links: `/latest`, `/archive`, `/notes`, `/feed.xml`,
  `/sponsor`. Style with `aria-current="page"` on the active link — that
  triggers the accent color + accent underline.
- 2px ink underline below; 40px margin-bottom.

## 2. `<PageGrid>` — sidebar + content shell

- CSS grid: `200px 1fr` with a 56px gap.
- Below `720px`, collapse to single column; sidebar moves to `order: 2`
  (after content).
- Used by every page that has a sidebar (all three so far).

## 3. `<Sidebar>` — site index column

- Mono, 12px, meta color.
- Sections each have a heading (`.sidebar__h`, ink color, semi-bold) and a
  vertical list with 8px gaps.
- Common headings: "Recent", "Tags", "Jump to", "Filter", "At a glance",
  "Past sponsors". Use whichever the page calls for.

## 4. `<Post>` — feed entry on Landing

```
<article class="post">
  <p class="post__dateline"><time datetime="…">MAY 22 2026</time></p>
  <h2 class="post__title">
    <a href="…">Title here</a>
    {/* if original essay: */}
    <span class="post__star" aria-label="Original post">★</span>
  </h2>
  <div class="post__body">…</div>
</article>
```

- Original essays get the `★`. Link posts don't.
- Post separator: `margin-top: 44px; padding-top: 40px; border-top: 1px
  solid var(--color-rule);` — applied via `.post + .post`.
- Body uses Newsreader serif; blockquotes get a 2px accent left rule and
  `var(--color-fg-muted)` text.

## 5. `<ArchiveRow>` — single archive entry

3-column grid `[56px date] [1fr title] [auto tag]` with a 16px gap.
Hairline `border-top` between rows. All mono. The tag is uppercase 10.5px
in meta color with `0.08em` letter-spacing.

## 6. `<RateRow>` — sponsorship rate

2-column `[1fr label] [auto price]`. Price is mono, 15px, semi-bold,
accent-colored. Hairline `border-top` between rows.

## 7. `<AvailabilityCal>` — sponsorship calendar

`grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr)` with 6px gap. Three cell states:
- `--available` — default, 1px ink border.
- `--next` — solid accent background, accent-fg text. Use sparingly (1–2
  cells max).
- `--sold` — 0.4 opacity, line-through.

Each cell shows a week label (e.g. "Jun 16") and a one-word status under
it.

## 8. `<CTA>` — primary call-to-action

Inline-block, 16px/24px padding, mono 13px, ink background, warm-white
text. On hover, swap to accent background and accent-fg text. Used once
per page max — currently only on the Sponsorship page.

---

## Reusability checklist

When you write a new page, you should be assembling these primitives — not
inventing new ones. If you find yourself reaching for a new component:

1. Can it be done with existing primitives + a token tweak? Do that.
2. If not, add the component here in this file first, with its props and
   class names, **before** building it.
